 "arrive_text": "The terrace runs right up to the wall now, a road of trampled earth and charred timber with the Roman sheds still standing along its sides. Beyond it Avaricum is quiet. Most of the roofs are gone. The wall stands, because it was built well, and the granaries stand, because the Romans wanted what was in them. It is raining, the way it rained the whole siege.",
